      "verdict": "unconfirmed",
      "reason": "summary-or-gloss-unfaithful",
      "note": "Wording, heading and position equal the card (column 2, Verhoudingen, second bullet). Gloss fault: the Dutch general term is \"verhoudingen\" (\"gesprekjes voeren over verhoudingen\"), and the gloss renders it \"proportions (*verhoudingen*, how sizes relate to each other)\". The bracket fixes the term to sizes, which is what the card's example (\"bijv. ... Wat is groter, een muis of een olifant?\") is about; the term itself also covers ratios between amounts, and an example is not a limit. The sibling record Verhoudingen / 1 has the same bracket but says in Limits \"Verhoudingen can also be read as ratios; the example given is about sizes\"; this record says so nowhere. Fix: give both readings in the bracket (for example \"how sizes or amounts relate to each other\"), or add to Limits the sentence Verhoudingen / 1 has.",
